1
00:00:04,218 --> 00:00:10,225
Indic AAC Studio: a symbol board in English, Hindi, Gujarati and Marathi. Selections go to a local server.

2
00:00:11,519 --> 00:00:16,524
1. Tap symbols. The shelf proposes next words from a trained infinity-gram model.

3
00:00:30,451 --> 00:00:38,455
2. The model proposed “I need food.”; the validator rejected it (selected concept missing) and the template returned “I want Water.”.

4
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:42,459
The card does not show whether the model or the template produced the sentence.

5
00:00:46,892 --> 00:00:51,896
Gujarati: “No” + “Water” (ના + પાણી). Labels exist in all four locales.

6
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:08,731
The validator accepted: “મને પાણી ના જોઈએ છે.” (negation kept).

7
00:01:12,957 --> 00:01:18,960
Intent-sensitive case: the feeling “Tired”. The web client infers intent from the labels and sends REQUEST.

8
00:01:26,193 --> 00:01:35,195
Accepted: “I'm feeling very tired. I need something to eat.”. The selected concept is present, but unselected content was added (a documented defect).

9
00:01:35,195 --> 00:01:43,199
Evaluation: 175 frozen scenarios, four languages. The gate lifts success from 37% to 55%; explicit polarity and intent fields give 75%.

10
00:01:43,199 --> 00:01:50,201
A template alone reaches 95% with explicit fields, so the gate is a safeguard, not a gain in sentence quality.

11
00:01:50,201 --> 00:01:56,204
Speech: the IndicF5 checkpoint is gated; this build returns a placeholder tone. A narrated take is pending.

12
00:01:56,204 --> 00:02:01,207
Package: source, fixtures, scorer and instructions. Download URL to be inserted at submission.
